 values the ticket already has changes nothing: no audit entry, and `updated` stays.
 
+### Assign a ticket: `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee`
+
+```json
+{ "assignee": "sam" }
+```
+
+`assignee` is an agent's name (not empty, at most 64 characters, one line) or `null` to unassign. Answers 200 with the ticket.
+Only `open` and `in_progress` tickets can be assigned or unassigned (409 `conflict` otherwise); a missing or invalid
+`assignee` is 400 `invalid`. Assigning the agent the ticket already has changes nothing: no audit entry, no notification,
+and `updated` stays. The agent is notified that the ticket was assigned to them; unassigning notifies nobody.
+
 ### Move a ticket along its lifecycle: `POST /tickets/:id/transition`
 
